==English==
{{wikipedia|Extraversion and introversion}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|extravert}}

===Etymology===
Alteration of earlier {{m|en|extravert}} (by influence of {{m|en|introvert}}), from {{bor|en|de|Extravert}}, popularized in psychology by Phyllis Blanchard's 1918 "Psycho-Analytic Study of August Comte".

